s I am religious that  has certain connotations that you will  have certain ideas or preconceived  notions about what that says about me  you my first  what I do in my life and so I try to  avoid saying that I am religious or not  religious if you were to ask me do I  believe in God I would usually say yes  but then even then I would have to  usually explain myself here in Sweden  there's kind of a stigma against  believing in God it's seen that's  rational and so I feel like I sometimes  have to if I say I believe in God and I  said well God to me means this and that  and so so it's a complex subject I'll  probably just leave it there and maybe  explain it further in the future when I  have a more thorough answer to give you  but am i religious it depends on what  you mean by that sir okay last question  for this video what sparked your  interest in religious studies I've  always been interested in religion  mythology in history and archaeology  it's a very fascinating subject you're  studying both historical subjects old  religions old civilizations and all this  but also today how religion affects  society religion impacts our lives and  and so on I didn't actually start my  academic career as as a student of  religions the first subject that I  studied was actually political science  not message oh because I wanted to  become a politician or anything but I  was looking to maybe work in NGOs or I  was so I had studied political science  for three semesters that I needed some  extra points to get my bachelor's degree  because I wasn't doing a full program  but individual courses and so I thought  well religion is interesting like I'm  interested in religion and so I took a  course in religion this is in 2015 and  just I think a few weeks into that  course I realized huh this may be this  was when I was supposed to be doing all  this time  it just piqued my interest and my  fascination on such a level and also not  sound like I'm bragging but I was also  they  good at it it just you just felt right  to me and so I kept studying that  feeling today I have a master's degree  and I'm looking to through I'm applying  currently for PhD positions so obviously  this is something that I'm very  interested in and then I want to  dedicate a large portion of my time to I  think I also realized as I was studying  religion not just how fascinating it is  in itself what its historical sort of  philosophical or metaphysical aspects  that's one thing but also because I  realized even more than I had before how  much society has impacted our society  our world generally how it still impacts  our world and our societies and our  lives basically how important religion  is to people in the world regardless if  we realize it or not but in spite of  this incredible importance it felt like  there is so much misconceptions about  religion people know very little about  how religion actually works what what  the history and the ideas of a lot of  these religions are it just felt like a  very important subject also for our  current world to understand religion  better means that we can talk to each  other better it means that we can  hopefully and eventually if we know more  about each other and each other's  religious traditions for example and  that opens up for more conversation and  more tolerance and so I just felt like  on the one hand is way very interesting  and fascinating subject on many  different ways but also that is a very  important subject and one that is very  beneficial both personally but also to  on a wider societal level so I think  that's in a nutshell why religious  studies seems so something that I wanted  to keep doing and that's all I have time  for today I hope you enjoyed that little  Q&amp;A if you want more videos like this I  suggest you like the video and maybe  leave a comment telling me if you want  more I will probably doing more of these  especially with my patrons and hopefully  as soon as I get my camera fixed I will  start  making the proper videos again it's  gonna take a little longer than usual I  try to release one video a week or at  least one every two weeks but this next  one might take a little longer so be  patient it is coming pretty soon until  then I hope you're all doing well and  I'll see you in the next video  [Music]

